# Assessment passes — read-first and output discipline

**Workflow:** **inputs** (`ASSESSMENT_INPUTS.md`) → **boundary** (`Assessment-Scope-V1_1.mdc` + `LATEST.md` bullets) → **score + backlog** (overwrite **`docs/assessments/LATEST.md`**) → **history** (`docs/archive/assessments/`, archived quality — comparison only). Do not cite archives as the current headline score.

When the prompt is an **architecture / readiness / weighted / first-principles / trust + product composite** assessment of this repository (not a narrow bugfix or single-feature change):

1. **Read [`docs/library/ASSESSMENT_INPUTS.md`](../../docs/library/ASSESSMENT_INPUTS.md)** — including **“One workflow (current score vs history)”** — and treat its table as the default evidence set before scanning thousands of sources.

   Repo-root shorthand: **`docs/library/ASSESSMENT_INPUTS.md`**.

   **GA / improvement execution:** when **`docs/library/CURSOR_PROMPTS_GA_TASK*.md`** exists for the improvement being executed (e.g. **`CURSOR_PROMPTS_GA_TASKS_27_32.md`**, **`CURSOR_PROMPTS_GA_TASK_26_AUTHORITY_DTF.md`**), treat that file as the **sequenced prompt source of record** — do not re-derive step lists solely from `LATEST.md` when the hand-authored prompts are richer.

2. **Apply** **`Assessment-Scope-V1_1.mdc`** explicitly — it is **not** always-loaded. In Cursor, **`@Assessment-Scope-V1_1`** / **`@.cursor/rules/Assessment-Scope-V1_1.mdc`**, or read the file directly. `(A)` vs `(B)` scoring boundary is mandatory for these passes.
3. **Write** the new assessment body to **`docs/assessments/LATEST.md`** (overwrite). Before overwriting, optional: copy the previous `LATEST.md` to **`docs/archive/assessments/`** with a dated filename.
   - **Top Improvement Opportunities — completed items:** **Do not remove** rows that are done. **Keep document order and numbering stable.** Mark the title line only as **`COMPLETED: <original title>`** (literal word **COMPLETED**, colon, space, then the same title text as before) so repeat assessment passes do not re-prompt shipped work. Optional one-line ship note may follow; **uneven detail across completed rows is fine** (no required ship date on every item). Defer long “closed” narratives to git history or archive snapshots. Actionable items stay **Yes** or **Deferred** as appropriate; completed rows use **Actionable: Completed** (or equivalent).
4. **Do not** treat **`docs/archive/assessments/**`** or historical narratives under **`docs/archive/quality/**`** as mandatory context unless the user asks for historical comparison — those paths are excluded from default indexing in **`.cursorignore`** where configured to reduce token burn on repeat passes.

For code-specific claims after the canonical doc pass, open **targeted** source files (controllers, orchestrators, ADRs) rather than whole-project file lists.
